[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#11DD11'> </div> !} AGL: {!</td><td>!} [+ farm_saxony_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ farm_r_saxony +]%  {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if not concord_formed: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#3E88B3'> </div> !} Traditionalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ traditionalist_saxony_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ traditionalist_r_saxony +]%  {!</td></tr>!} ?]

[? if dnf_formed : {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#003755'> </div> !}CNF: {!</td><td>!} [+ dnf_saxony_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ dnf_r_saxony +]%  {!</td></tr>!} ?]

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#7A3C00'> </div> !} Royalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ royalist_saxony_elections_vote +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ royalist_r_saxony +]%  {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}
<hr id="read-marker">
[? if aspd_dead and reformists_resign: Despite the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>'s reunion with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> after the state Assembly election 4 years ago, our party's leftist direction at the federal level has driven them to split off again. ?]
[? if royalist_r_saxony > (royalist_r_saxony_old + 5) and not saxony_royalist: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> have made significant gains relative to last election.  This may make a stable governing arrangement more difficult this time around. ?]
[? if saxony_royalist: Following Garrick Crowde's anti-capitalist antics of the previous coalition, the propertied parties are quite reluctant to include the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in government again. ?]
<hr id="read-marker">
United Left Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #C43988;">**CPO**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?]): [+ left_coalition_saxony +]% 

Unity Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if unionist_r_saxony:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> ?][? if not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+&nbsp;<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]): [+ marcher_coalition_saxony +]% 

[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Propertied Coalition ([? if unionist_r_saxony: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if vnr_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #D3D3A9;">**PNA**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #11DD11;">**AGL**</span> + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**ECP**</span> + <span style="color: #0075EB;">**PRP**</span>[? if csvd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**FSP**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>): [+ true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony +]% ?]

[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": Propertied Coalition ([? if unionist_r_saxony: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if vnr_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #D3D3A9;">**PNA**</span> ?] + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**ECP**</span> + <span style="color: #0075EB;">**PRP**</span>[? if csvd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**FSP**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?]): [+ true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony +]% ?]

[? if saxony_no_majority_2: Right-wing Coalition ([? if unionist_r_saxony: <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + ?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] + <span style="color: #b8996f;">**ECP**</span> + <span style="color: #0075EB;">**PRP**</span>[? if kvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?] + <span style="color: #11DD11;">**AGL**</span> + <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> + <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>): [+ true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony +]% ?]

@saxony_coalition_menu
on-arrival: {!
let dvp_toleration_threshold = 30;
let lvp_toleration_threshold = 40;
if (Q.gold_leader == "Coalfax") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Mardle") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 20;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Holt") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Vellt") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
} else if (Q.gold_leader == "Curthose") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.gold_ideology != "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.gold_ideology == "Left") {
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
}
if (Q.lvp_leader == "Coalfax") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Quill") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Marsh") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Tinsmore") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Hewes") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 10;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Vellt") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
} else if (Q.lvp_leader == "Dietrich") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology != "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold += 5;
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (Q.left_coalition_saxony >= 50) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 15;
}
if (Q.saxony_groko) {
    lvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
    dvp_toleration_threshold -= 5;
}
if (!Q.gold_exist || (Q.gold_relation >= dvp_toleration_threshold && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= lvp_toleration_threshold && Q.lvp_formed)) {
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.toleration_possible_saxony = 0;
}
if (((Q.unionist_relation >= 50 || !Q.stegerwald_path || (Q.unionist_relation >= 45 && Q.saxony_groko)) && ((Q.ddp_relation >= (lvp_toleration_threshold + 10) && !Q.gold_exist)) || (Q.gold_relation >= (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation >= (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed))) {
    Q.marcher_coalition_possible_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.marcher_coalition_possible_saxony = 0;
}
if ((Q.gold_relation < (dvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && !Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.lvp_relation < (lvp_toleration_threshold + 5) && Q.lvp_formed)) {
    Q.gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony = 1;
} else {
    Q.gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony = 0;
}
!}

# Reminder of possible coalition outcomes from 1929/1930 Dornish elections:
# Hale toleration, Sheckley toleration, Hale groko, 1930 Groko, Successful United Left, United Left Commonwealth intervention, Marchers majority, Sheckley majority, Royalists enter
# Relevant variables: saxony_toleration, saxony_groko, red_saxony, saxony_joever, saxony_spd, saxony_right_2, saxony_nsdap

- @continue_toleration_saxony
- @continue_groko_saxony
- @continue_spd_majority
- @continue_left_saxony
- @continue_borko_saxony
- @new_grand_coalition_saxony
- @toleration_saxony
- @true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony
- @united_left_saxony
- @no_majority
- @spd_majority
- @ddp_saxony
- @soclib_saxony_cvp
- @far_right_coalition_saxony
- @far_left_saxony
- @nazi_saxony
- @no_majority_spd

# Coalitions are still a work in progress for sure.  Initial ones down here are just the 1930 text repeated, plus a little more.

@continue_left_saxony
title: We will continue our coalition with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">**United**</span> <span style="color: #c00000;">**Front**</span> marches on.
view-if: left_coalition_saxony >= 50 and red_saxony
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 25 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or (collectivist_relation >= 45 and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators")
unavailable-subtitle: Our parties' relations have deteriorated too far.
on-arrival: red_saxony = 1; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; gold_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; coup_progress += 3; dufour_angry += 30; vanguard_militancy += 0.04; vanguard_strength += 100; loyalist_strength += 40; warden_strength += 40; strife += 1; commons_marcher += 3; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; landed_marcher -= 3; communist_coalition += 2; collectivist_relation += 10; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

<span style="color: #c00000;">**Red**</span> Dornwich is maintained.  The propertied parties hate us all the more, but their cries are ineffectual.  We will continue transforming the state into a stronghold of <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>.

[? if coup_progress >= 8: Amidst our electoral victory, a far-right coup attempt is rumored to be close at hand.  Proceed with caution. ?]

@continue_borko_saxony
title: The propertied parties have retained their parliamentary majority.
view-if: true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50 and saxony_right_2
on-arrival: saxony_right_2 = 1; pro_republic += 1; landed_royalist -= 1; guild_royalist -= 1; commons_marcher -= 1; commons_ddp += 1 if not lvp_formed; commons_lvp += 1 if lvp_formed; landed_other += 1 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_other += 1 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; landed_traditionalist += 1 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist += 1 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Once again, the propertied parties have secured a majority all on their own.

The continued propertied strength is demoralizing both to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and to us, as we are once again relegated to the powerless opposition role. 

@ddp_saxony
title: We will form a coalition with only the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if reformists_resign or not aspd_dead: and the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>?].
subtitle: With the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> having lurched to the right, this may be a viable option.
view-if: (marcher_r_saxony + aspd_r_saxony + ddp_r_saxony >= 50) and gold_exist and not toleration_possible_saxony
choose-if: ddp_relation >= 100 and ddp_ideology == "Left" and not bourgeois_parliament_ddp and liberal_cooperation < 10
unavailable-subtitle: [? if ddp_relation < 100: We need higher relations with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>. ?][? if ddp_ideology != "Left": The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Dornish chapter is too right-wing to agree to this. ?][? if bourgeois_parliament_ddp or liberal_cooperation >= 10: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is still too closely tied with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to agree to this. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_groko = 0; saxony_toleration = 0; commons_royalist -= 4; disfavored_royalist -= 4; commons_marcher += 4; disfavored_marcher += 3; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; commons_ddp += 3; disfavored_ddp += 3; ddp_relation += 3; pro_republic += 5; reformist_dissent -= 10; reformist_strength += 5; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 1; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Somehow, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is willing to form a coalition with us, without the increasingly <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> on board.

@soclib_saxony_cvp
title: We will form a coalition with only the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>[? if reformists_resign or not aspd_dead: and the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span>?].
subtitle: With the <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> having lurched to the right, this may be a viable option.
view-if: true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and (marcher_r_saxony + aspd_r_saxony + ddp_r_saxony + gold_r_saxony + lvp_r_saxony >= 50) and concord_formed and concord_coalition_right
choose-if: (gold_relation >= 60 and gold_ideology == "Left" and not lvp_formed and gold_exist) or (lvp_relation >= 70 and lvp_ideology != "Right" and lvp_formed) or (ddp_relation >= 70 and not gold_exist)
unavailable-subtitle: We need higher relations with the [? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if gold_exist and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not gold_exist: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?].
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_groko = 0; saxony_toleration = 0; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; burgher_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; gold_relation += 5; pro_republic += 3; reformist_dissent -= 10; reformist_strength += 5; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 1; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Somehow, the liberals are willing to form a coalition with us, without the increasingly <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> on board.

@far_left_saxony
title: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> will form a government[? if sapd_formed: with the <span style="color: #9B0000;">Laborists</span>?], with or without our participation.
subtitle: Beyond all expectation.
view-if: collectivist_r_saxony + sapd_r_saxony >= 50
on-arrival: dataminer_detected = 1; collectivist_reichsex_sax = 1; collectivist_relation = 65; commons_collectivist += 5; commons_sapd += 5 if sapd_formed

None thought such a thing possible.  

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> immediately launches a coup attempt against the new Dornish government.  And all know what follows.

- @civil_war

@nazi_saxony
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> forms a majority government.
subtitle: We are so cooked... 
view-if: royalist_r_saxony >= 50
on-arrival: gallax_explode = time + 36; saxony_royalist_maj = 1; royalist_left += 5; pro_republic -= 10; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0; data_miner_detected = 1; commons_royalist += 12; commons_collectivist -= 6; commons_marcher -= 4; disfavored_royalist += 12; disfavored_collectivist -= 6; disfavored_marcher -= 4; burgher_royalist += 8; burgher_ddp -= 2; burgher_lvp -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 6; loyalist_strength += 200; loyalist_militancy += 0.1; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.1
go-to: president_hate if (president_ideology == "Left") and not presidential_powers; president_allow if (president_ideology != "Left") and not presidential_powers; president_oops if presidential_powers
face-image: img/portraits/strasser.jpg

The worst has come to pass in Dornwich: an <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> majority.  Garrick Crowde becomes the new minister-president.

Dornwich, once a stronghold of <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span> and democracy, is now being dismantled by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. The "democratic" aspect more so, as Crowde has adopted relatively pro-worker and anti-capitalist policies, at least compared to the propertied parties.  The state police, now almost entirely <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, are actively suppressing <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>, <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span>, and even <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> organizations and meetings.  Newspapers critical of the government have been banned, and civil servants with suspected <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> or <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democratic</span> leanings are being purged in large numbers.

@president_oops

Thanks to our own constitutional amendment, the president no longer has the power to call Commonwealth Interventions, and we are thus powerless to prevent this development.

@president_allow

Despite his significant disagreements with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, President [+ president +] is not willing to do anything about their takeover of Dornwich.

@president_hate
go-to: pres_kpd if (president == "Munzer" or president == "Halsmark"); pres_spd if president_ideology == "Left" and not (president == "Munzer" or president == "Halsmark")

@pres_kpd
on-arrival: collectivist_reichsex_sax = 1; collectivist_relation = 65

There is absolutely no way that President [+ president +] is going to let this stand, and he has ordered a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> against the Dornish government.  Expectedly, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> refuse to stand down.

- @civil_war

@pres_spd

President [+ president +] now faces a dilemma.  As terrible as they are, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> <i>did</i> win a majority, so do they not have a mandate to govern?  Moreover, they will almost certainly resist any attempted <i>Commonwealth intervention</i>, triggering a civil war.

- @yes
- @no

@no
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> have won the day.  Let them govern.
subtitle: We are not willing to risk a civil war at this time.

@yes
title: The power of <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> exists for a reason, and times like this call for it.
subtitle: President [+ president +] will remove Crowde's cabinet, by force if necessary.

Expectedly, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> refuse to stand down.

- @civil_war

@no_majority_spd
title: No majority can be found!
subtitle: [? if true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and marcher_coalition_saxony < 50: All possible coalitions lack a majority. ?][? if marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and not marcher_coalition_possible_saxony: The propertied parties are antagonistic to our Dornish organization. ?][? if marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and left_strength >= 25: Our party itself rejects the possibility of a majority coalition with the liberals. ?]
view-if: saxony_marcher_maj and true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and (marcher_coalition_saxony < 50 or ((not marcher_coalition_possible_saxony or left_strength >= 25) and marcher_r_saxony < 50)) and (collectivist_r_saxony + sapd_r_saxony) < 50 and royalist_r_saxony < 50

With our decline in popularity, and our party and the propertied refusing to govern together, the state Assembly is in a deadlock. Our Cabinet remains in power as a caretaker government, but a simple majority vote can still dissolve the state Assembly.

[? if mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50: The coalition of parties in between the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and the anti-democratic Right constitute a majority, but given our animosity, it is unclear if we will be able to prevent new elections from being called. ?][? if mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50: The coalition of parties in between the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and the anti-democratic Right don't even constitute a majority, making any majority government impossible. ?]

- @toleration_saxony
- @sapd_aspd_ddp
- @no_majority_2

@sapd_aspd_ddp
title: Perhaps our splinter parties and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> could be persuaded, in the name of stability?
view-if: marcher_r_saxony + sapd_r_saxony + aspd_r_saxony + ddp_r_saxony >= 50 
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 30 or (marcher_r_saxony + aspd_r_saxony + ddp_r_saxony >= 50 and ddp_relation >= 80)) and ((ddp_relation >= 80 and (ddp_ideology == "Left") and left_strength < 20 and saxony_marcher) or (ddp_relation >= 60 and marcher_r_saxony + sapd_r_saxony + aspd_r_saxony >= 50) or (marcher_r_saxony + sapd_r_saxony >= 50))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if collectivist_relation < 30 and sapd_formed: The <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> refuses. ?][? if ddp_relation < 60 and (reformists_resign or not aspd_dead): The <span style="color: #fe9e00;">**ORP**</span> refuses. ?][? if (ddp_relation < 80 or ddp_ideology != "Left" or not marcher_r_saxony or left_strength >= 20) and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> refuses. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_marcher_splinter = 1; pro_republic += 1; guild_ddp -= 2; burgher_ddp -= 2; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

We have cobbled together a majority coalition with other constitutional left-of-center parties.  Hopefully it lasts.

@continue_spd_majority
title: We maintain our majority government.
subtitle: The expected course of action.
view-if: saxony_marcher_maj
choose-if: marcher_r_saxony >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: We have lost our majority in the state Assembly.
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 20; left_strength += 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; aspd_dead = 1; commons_marcher += 5; commons_collectivist -= 3; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher += 1; disfavored_marcher += 3; disfavored_royalist -= 2; pro_republic += 4; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0;

We have maintained our solo majority in the Dornish state Assembly.  This has all but cemented us as the natural governing party of Dornwich.

@continue_toleration_saxony
title: We will continue our toleration agreement with the incumbent government.
view-if: saxony_toleration
choose-if: toleration_possible_saxony and mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50 and left_strength < 35 and marcher_r_saxony < 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not toleration_possible_saxony: The propertied parties won't even accept our toleration anymore. ?][? if mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50: Our toleration is no longer sufficient to secure a majority. ?][? if left_strength >= 35: Our Dornish chapter is refusing to cooperate. Again. ?][? if marcher_r_saxony >= 50: An <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> majority is now possible. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_toleration = 1; pro_republic += 1; left_dissent += 10; commons_collectivist += 2; commons_sapd += 2 if sapd_formed; commons_marcher -= 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; disfavored_sapd += 3 if sapd_formed; disfavored_marcher -= 5; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Our toleration agreement in Dornwich continues.  Our party's remaining leftist elements grow weary of this arrangement, and they are increasingly defecting to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> [? if sapd_formed: and <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?].  Nevertheless, we have at least avoided repeat elections.

@continue_groko_saxony
title: The [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition is maintained!
subtitle: We remain on good terms with the propertied parties, and as such they're willing to govern with us again.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if marcher_coalition_saxony < 50: The [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition has lost its majority. ?][? if unionist_relation < 45 and stegerwald_path: Our relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] have deteriorated too far. ?][? if gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony: Our relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?] have deteriorated too far. ?][? if left_strength >= 30: Our Dornish chapter is refusing to cooperate. Again. ?][? if left_strength >= 15 and marcher_r_saxony >= 50: We neither need nor want to include the propertied in government any longer. ?]
view-if: saxony_groko
choose-if: marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and marcher_coalition_possible_saxony and left_strength < 30 and (concord_coalition_left or (concord_coalition_moderate and far_right_coalition_saxony < 50 and bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50) or not concord_formed) and (marcher_r_saxony < 50 or left_strength < 15)
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_groko = 1; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; unionist_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; gold_relation += 5; pro_republic += 3; reformist_dissent -= 15; reformist_strength += 10; aspd_dead = 1; saxony_toleration = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Once again, the propertied parties are willing to form a [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition with us.

This development has weakened the[? if royalist_r_saxony < 10: already-struggling ?]<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, [? if royalist_r_saxony > royalist_r_saxony_old: who were hoping to use their increased popularity to force their way into government this time around?]. 

@new_grand_coalition_saxony
title: A [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition is formed!
subtitle: We have finally reconciled with the propertied parties, and they're willing to govern with us again.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if red_saxony: The propertied are not ready to forgive us for coalitioning with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. ?][? if unionist_relation < 50 and stegerwald_path: We need higher relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if gold_toleration_threshold_fail_saxony: We need higher relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>?]. ?][? if left_strength >= 25: Our Dornish organization is too left-wing to even consider this as an option—after all, their stubborn refusal in the past led to the expulsion of the majority of the parliamentary faction and the subsequent formation of the <span style="color: #fe9e00;">ORP</span>. ?][? if concord_formed: The <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> refuses to work with us. ?]
view-if: marcher_coalition_saxony >= 50 and not saxony_groko
choose-if: marcher_coalition_possible_saxony and left_strength < 25 and (concord_coalition_left or (concord_coalition_moderate and far_right_coalition_saxony < 50 and bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50) or not concord_formed) and not red_saxony
on-arrival: saxony_marcher = 1; saxony_groko = 1; saxony_toleration = 0; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; unionist_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; gold_relation += 5; pro_republic += 3; reformist_dissent -= 15; reformist_strength += 10; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Somehow, the propertied parties are willing to form a [? if lvp_formed and stegerwald_path: Unity?][? if not lvp_formed or not stegerwald_path: Grand?] Coalition with us this time around.

This development has weakened the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, who are now relegated to the powerless opposition.

@toleration_saxony
title: We will enter a toleration agreement with the propertied parties.
view-if: not saxony_toleration and marcher_r_saxony < 50
choose-if: mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50 and true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50: Our votes won't matter, as the anti-democratic parties hold a majority. ?][? if true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50: They don't need our toleration. ?]
on-arrival: saxony_toleration = 1; saxony_groko = 0; pro_republic += 2; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Unfortunately, we have been relegated to toleration of the propertied parties.   
The Sheckley Cabinet is re-established, composed only of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if stegerwald_path: and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]?].

@far_right_coalition_saxony
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> enters the governing coalition.
subtitle: Unfortunately, there is no other viable option.
view-if: saxony_no_majority_2
choose-if: mega_bourgeois_coalition_saxony < 50 and far_right_coalition_saxony >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Even when including the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, the propertied government can't find a majority.
on-arrival: saxony_royalist = 1; royalist_left += 5; gallax_explode = time + 36; data_miner_detected = 1; commons_royalist += 6; commons_collectivist -= 3; commons_marcher -= 2; disfavored_royalist += 6; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 4; burgher_ddp -= 1; burgher_lvp -= 1; burgher_marcher -= 3; loyalist_strength += 100; loyalist_militancy += 0.05; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; pro_republic -= 5; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0
go-to: reichsex_dilemma if president_ideology == "Left" and not presidential_powers
face-image: img/portraits/strasser.jpg

After a failed negotiation previously, the propertied parties are now willing to offer a ministerial position to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in exchange for their support. Garrick Crowde, leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>'s left wing, has been appointed as the new Interior Minister, a role he had been denied in the past due to his more radical anti-capitalist views.

Dornwich, once a stronghold of <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span> and democracy, is now being dismantled by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. The "democratic" aspect more so, as Crowde has pushed for the cabinet to adopt pro-worker and anti-capitalist policies in an attempt to win their votes. The state police, now largely comprised of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, are actively suppressing <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span> organizations and meetings. Reformist newspapers critical of the government have been banned, and civil servants with suspected <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> or <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democratic</span> leanings are being purged in large numbers.

However, there is a real possibility that Crowde could be removed from his position by his coalition partners, as they were never a huge fan of him.

@reichsex_dilemma

President [+ president +] is considering the use of a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> to stop the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> terror in Dornwich.  This might risk a civil war, however.  Even if it succeeds, we'll likely just end up in an election loop again.

- @do
- @dont

@do
title: The power of <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> exists for a reason, and times like this call for it.
subtitle: President [+ president +] will remove Crowde from his post, by force if necessary.
on-arrival: pres_strength = banner_strength*banner_militancy*(1-dissent/2); enemy_strength = loyalist_strength*loyalist_militancy + warden_strength*warden_militancy; pres_strength += army_strength*army_loyalty*army_militancy; pres_strength += vanguard_strength*vanguard_militancy if (president == "Munzer" or president == "Halsmark"); pres_strength += vanguard_strength*vanguard_militancy*(collectivist_relation/100) if (collectivist_truce or in_popular_front or in_left_front or in_popular_front_heartland or in_left_front_heartland) and president != "Munzer" and president != "Halsmark"
go-to: pres_victory if pres_strength >= enemy_strength; war if pres_strength < enemy_strength

@pres_victory
on-arrival: saxony_royalist = 0; commons_royalist -= 4; disfavored_royalist -= 4; burgher_royalist -= 4; guild_royalist -= 4; landed_royalist -= 4; loyalist_strength -= 100; loyalist_militancy *= 0.8; coup_progress -= 3; pro_republic += 2; saxony_1933_trigger_time = time + 3

Crowde has backed down!  Unfortunately, as there was no other viable path to a coalition in the state Assembly, it will need to be dissolved for new elections once more.

@war
on-arrival: collectivist_relation = 65 if president == "Munzer" or president == "Halsmark"; collectivist_reichsex_sax = 1 if president == "Munzer" or president == "Halsmark"

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> refuse to acquiesce.  

- @civil_war: This is civil war.

@dont
title: We must not risk a civil war over Dornwich.
subtitle: We will let the cabinet stand.

Hopefully Crowde's tenure will prove short-lived.

@true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony
title: The propertied parties have garnered a majority to rule via parliament.
view-if: true_bourgeois_coalition_saxony >= 50 and not saxony_right_2
on-arrival: saxony_right_2 = 1; pro_republic += 2; landed_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_other += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_other += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; landed_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; red_saxony = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0

Surprisingly, the propertied parties have secured a majority all on their own.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> is heavily demoralized by this defeat, as they are relegated to the powerless opposition role. They had expected the national political climate to benefit them, and to allow them to influence government.

@united_left_saxony
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> will form a coalition government with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
subtitle: Will history repeat itself?
view-if: left_coalition_saxony >= 50 and (collectivist_relation >= 35 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or (collectivist_relation >= 55 and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators") and not red_saxony
on-arrival: red_saxony = 1; unionist_relation -= 7; ddp_relation -= 7; gold_relation -= 7; lvp_relation -= 7; coup_progress += 5; dufour_angry += 60; vanguard_militancy += 0.08; vanguard_strength += 150; loyalist_strength += 80; warden_strength += 80; strife += 1; commons_marcher += 5; commons_collectivist += 5; disfavored_marcher += 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; guild_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 5; communist_coalition += 3; collectivist_relation += 15; saxony_toleration = 0; saxony_groko = 0; saxony_joever = 0; saxony_marcher = 0; saxony_right_2 = 0; saxony_royalist = 0; saxony_marcher_splinter = 0; saxony_soclib = 0; saxony_royalist_maj = 0; saxony_collectivist = 0; saxony_marcher_maj = 0
